From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:27:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 581/581] [DS4.1] L2 prefetch: the owner and Engram layers'
 windows placed where their lines survive

A layer that owns a compressor lost its WO lines to the compressor's
projection before WO-A ran (WO-A at DRAM speed with its fill long done). It
now issues a COMP window (the compressor's weight) after Q-B in WO's place, and
WO right after the compressor.

An Engram layer runs its projection before anything the NEXT window holds,
and NEXT's lines did not survive it. The layer before it issues an ENGRAM
window (the projection's first 20 MB) in NEXT's place, and the Engram layer
issues NEXT between its projection's GEMM and its all-gather
(common/engram.py: project_rows, the hook between the two).

Forty decode layers at one rank's shapes on GB10 (real projections and routed
experts, spin kernels for the attention core and all-reduces): TP4 1.5% faster
at one stream, 0.7% at eight, 0.3% at sixteen; TP3 1.5 / 0.5 / 0.3%; every
buffer bit-identical. Cache hints only.
